Your client entrypoint is in the wrong place in `default.project.json`. `src/client/init.client.luau` is currently mapped to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`, and LocalScripts don't run from `ReplicatedStorage`, so `print("client")` would never execute.

The fix is to map the client folder under `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts` instead:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "StarterPlayer": {
      "StarterPlayerScripts": {
        "Client": { "$path": "src/client" }
      }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } }
  }
}
```

The file stays at `src/client/init.client.luau`. Rojo turns it into a LocalScript named `Client` under `StarterPlayerScripts`, which is what runs on each client. The server side is already correct: `src/server/init.server.luau` becomes a Script under `ServerScriptService`.

Code that both sides need goes in `src/shared`, which is fine in `ReplicatedStorage`. I haven't changed the project file. Do you want me to apply this edit?
